;; SBSA reference platform with the standard userspace.
;;
;; target:qemu-aarch64-sbsa was imported from Buildroot's own defconfig — nobody
;; hand-tuned it for this. Its boot chain is ARM Trusted Firmware, then EDK2,
;; then GRUB2 off an EFI partition on a GPT disk, and the kernel enumerates
;; hardware through ACPI rather than devicetree. Nothing like the Odroid's
;; Amlogic chain or the Pi's VideoCore firmware.
;;
;; profile:standard and feature:networking are the same fragments those images
;; use, unedited. That is the claim: a server platform and an Amlogic SBC can
;; share a userspace definition, because the axes are separable.
;;
;; Verified: 32 buildroot symbols and 14 linux symbols honoured by kbuild, and
;; it boots to a systemd login with no failed units.

(image sbsa-standard
  (compose
    target:qemu-aarch64-sbsa
    profile:standard
    feature:networking)
  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
